\caption{What the green extension does to the coordinated band (schematic,
one cycle repeated). Green bars are the coordinated main-street green at three
junctions in route order; red is the rest of the cycle. Dots mark the bus at
each junction, coloured by the aspect it meets. (a) Without action the bus
arrives at J1 after its green, is held for the red, and then meets the next
band at each downstream junction, losing time at every stop. (b) With the
extension the bus passes J1 inside the current band and crosses J2 and J3
without stopping. The downstream bands are unchanged: the extension removes
the stop and keeps the bus in the wave, which is the time it saves.}
