\section{The Exact Scheduling Program (MILP)}
\label{sec:milp}
% ==============================================================================

This section presents the complete mixed-integer linear program.  It is
deliberately written as a \emph{full-horizon} decision
problem: a controller with perfect advance knowledge of every bus and
car arrival, queue formation, and signal state over the entire planning
horizon could enact its solution verbatim, and no sequence of TSP actions
could outperform it.  The program therefore serves two roles: it is the
normative definition of what \emph{should} be done at every intersection in
every step, and it is the yardstick against which all controllers are
measured.

