chosen, and what constrains the choice.  Nothing here is new mathematics;
every row points to its defining equation.

\paragraph{Problem summary.}
Choose, for every intersection and every integer second, which phase is green
($x$), which TSP event forces it ($y$/$s$), where each clock sits ($\phi$),
and when each bus arrives ($\tau$, vacuous if none)--so that the single
scalar of \cref{eq:opt_crit} is minimised.  The criterion is total passenger
delay (\cref{tab:objective_terms}); progression is an addable linear term, and
lateness and corridor travel time are caps. It
returns a Gantt schedule
